## Integration recipes

### n8n

- **Call the API:** *HTTP Request* node → Authentication *Generic Credential Type* → *Header Auth*, Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer dpk_xxx`. URL form: `https://<domain>/api/v1/...`.
- **Receive events:** *Webhook* node (POST), turn on Options → *Raw Body*. Copy the Production URL, then register it with `POST /api/v1/webhooks`. Verify the signature with a *Crypto* node (HMAC, SHA256, hex) over the string `<X-Deplao-Timestamp>.<original body>`.
- **Example:** new order (Webhook from your sales website) → *HTTP Request* `POST /api/v1/accounts/{account_id}/conversations/{thread_id}/messages` with the body `{"text": "Thank you for your order #{{$json.order_id}}"}`.

### Make (Integromat)

- **Call the API:** *HTTP → Make a request* module, header `Authorization: Bearer dpk_xxx`, Body type *Raw*, Content type *JSON (application/json)*.
- **Receive events:** *Webhooks → Custom webhook*, copy the address, then register a Deplao webhook with the `events` you need. If the scenario cannot verify signatures itself, keep the webhook address secret (Make generates a long random address) and use HTTPS only.

### Google Apps Script / Google Sheets

Apps Script cannot read the headers of incoming requests (so it cannot verify signatures) and returns 302 for POST, so **do not use webhooks**. Use polling with a time-driven trigger instead (Triggers → Time-driven → every minute):

```js
const BASE = 'https://<domain>/api/v1';

function pollDeplao() {
  const props = PropertiesService.getScriptProperties();
  const key = props.getProperty('DEPLAO_KEY');
  const since = Number(props.getProperty('since') || 0);
  const res = UrlFetchApp.fetch(BASE + '/events?types=message.received&limit=200&since=' + since, {
    headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + key },
    muteHttpExceptions: true,
  });
  const body = JSON.parse(res.getContentText());
  if (!body.success) throw new Error(body.error.code + ': ' + body.error.message);
  const sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActive().getSheetByName('Messages');
  body.data.forEach(function (ev) {
    const conv = ev.data.conversation || {};
    const msg = ev.data.message || {};
    sheet.appendRow([new Date(ev.ts), ev.account_id, conv.display_name, msg.text]);
  });
  props.setProperty('since', String(body.pagination.next_since));
}
```

### Worker or your own server (calling the API)

```js
const res = await fetch('https://<domain>/api/v1/accounts/0501234567/conversations/8765432109876/messages', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.DEPLAO_KEY,
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Idempotency-Key': 'order-1001-shipped', // send the same key again → no duplicate message
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ text: 'Order #1001 has been delivered to the shipper', thread_type: 'user' }),
});
const out = await res.json();
if (!out.success) console.error(out.error.code, out.error.message);
```

- `Idempotency-Key` is remembered for 24 hours (until the app restarts). Sending the same key again returns the first result unchanged.
- Group chat: `"thread_type": "group"`.

